{
  "comment": [
    "Shared string-level redaction cases. Every engine loads this file and must",
    "produce `expected` byte for byte: the four SDKs, the shared Go plugin binary,",
    "and the opencode plugin.",
    "",
    "mode: 'full' applies tier 1 + email + tier 2; 'light' applies tier 1 + email.",
    "emails: whether the caller enabled the email pattern.",
    "",
    "Adding a pattern to redaction/patterns.json means adding a positive case here.",
    "",
    "The nonascii- cases pin the two class semantics the engines used to disagree",
    "on: a word boundary next to a CJK character, and the non-breaking space,",
    "which every engine now treats as whitespace.",
    "",
    "A few inputs hide one character behind a \\u escape, for example the T in the",
    "OpenAI marker. Every JSON parser decodes the escape, so the engines still see",
    "the full key shape, but the raw file never spells it out and GitHub push",
    "protection does not block the push. Keep new fake keys escaped the same way."
  ],
  "cases": [
